Now it is the lunch break.
I go outside the office.
There is a mobile shop near the office.
I go to the shop.
A shopkeeper is there.
I speak to the shopkeeper.
"Hello, brother."
"I need a new SIM card."
The shopkeeper asks me.
"Madam, do you have an old Indian SIM card?"
I say.
"No, I do not have an Indian SIM card."
"I am from Mexico."
"Therefore, I want a new SIM card."
The shopkeeper smiles.
He says.
"Okay, madam."
"I give a new SIM card."
